From fc72cba56d796343b494e90e6b95f921772c7a0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:37:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] virtio/fs: a share with simplified permissions

FsDevice::new_simplified (krun_fs_device_new_simplified) makes a writable
share with PermissionSemantics::LinuxSimplified, which the C API couldn't
select: every file shows as owned by the guest process asking and
permission bits are the host file's own mode, so a guest user whose uid
isn't the host user's can write the host user's folders without the
override xattr landing on them. Such a share serves no extended attributes
either, as the semantics' own documentation says, so the guest can't
store any on the host's files; that includes the security context a
create, mkdir, mknod or symlink request carries, which the macOS
passthrough stored as security.selinux even on a share without xattrs.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
